PDFium / Foxit Standard 14 PDF substitute fonts
==============================================

Copyright 2014 The PDFium Authors
Original code copyright 2014 Foxit Software Inc. http://www.foxitsoftware.com
The upstream chromefontdata.h also carries Copyright 2015 The PDFium Authors.

These 14 CFF font programs are byte-for-byte extractions of the corresponding
kFoxit*FontData arrays in PDFium's core/fxge/fontdata/chromefontdata/Foxit*.cpp.
Every selected source file explicitly identifies its license as BSD-style and
refers to the upstream LICENSE. The complete upstream LICENSE is preserved here
(source bundle: LICENSE; installed font directory: LICENSE.pdfium). It includes
the BSD redistribution conditions and disclaimer, and the upstream appended
Apache License 2.0 text. No separate font-license override was present in the
selected upstream source files or chromefontdata directory at this revision.

Upstream repository: https://github.com/chromium/pdfium
Pinned revision: a84323421e94f484faca52dd9d027934eba42ab8
Source directory: core/fxge/fontdata/chromefontdata
Source URL prefix:
https://github.com/chromium/pdfium/tree/a84323421e94f484faca52dd9d027934eba42ab8/core/fxge/fontdata/chromefontdata

The original source arrays and notices are retained in the source distribution.
Only the hexadecimal array initializers are decoded; outlines, names, widths,
encodings, and internal font metadata are not edited. FoxitSansMM and
FoxitSerifMM are not included. prepare_fonts.py documents and reproduces the
mechanical extraction. manifest.json records source and output SHA-256 hashes
and the explicit PDF Base14-to-file mapping. The runtime copy of this manifest
is named base14-manifest.json.

These files are application-private PDF substitutes, not Microsoft or Adobe
font files, and are not installed into the operating system. Their inclusion
does not imply endorsement by Google, PDFium contributors, or Foxit Software.
